menu "Michi Music Stream Display"

    config MICHI_DISPLAY_TASK_STACK_BYTES
        int "Display render task stack (bytes)"
        default 4096
        range 2048 16384
        help
          Stack of the render task (ESP-IDF xTaskCreate takes bytes). The
          task draws into the PSRAM framebuffer and flushes it to the panel
          (a full-frame flush is ~65-80 ms at 20 MHz SPI), so the stack also
          covers the esp_lcd draw_bitmap call. Raise it only if a future
          screen needs deeper frames.

    config MICHI_DISPLAY_QUEUE_LEN
        int "Render request queue length (requests)"
        default 4
        range 2 32
        help
          Depth of the FreeRTOS queue between the state observer /
          update_now_playing / request_redraw producers and the render task.
          A request dropped while the queue is full is logged (warn) by the
          producer and sets a pending flag; the task re-renders once more
          after the drain when the flag is set, and the next state change
          re-renders anyway, so a dropped request does not leave the screen
          stale (a drop racing that re-render is covered by the next state
          change).

    config MICHI_DISPLAY_RASTER_2BIT
        bool "Enable 2-bit anti-aliased raster mode"
        default n
        help
          Enable 2-bit AA raster mode. Requires regenerating assets with --raster 2bit. Disabled by default pending hardware display validation.

endmenu
